cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or the code behind it, please cite it as below."
title: "Payload retrieval under a holdout: a benchmark for decomposition in function-based screening"
abstract: >-
  A retrieval benchmark that asks whether function-based (embedding) screening needs a
  decomposition step in a way local alignment does not. Each item supplies one protein,
  the payload-bearing ORF as a naive six-frame caller emitted it, and a 40,750-protein
  catalogue, and asks for a ranking. The benchmark then removes the payload's close
  relatives at six identity thresholds and reads where the best surviving relative lands.
  1,102 items over four tiers, stratified by payload fraction, with two baselines and the
  scoring rules shipped as code.
